<<<
the use of pre-war as an adverb
===
the use of *pre-war* as an adverb
>>>

<<<
that use of before the war, which
===
that use of *before the war*, which
>>>

<<<
shown— The suggestion is utterly untrue, as a comparison of present prices with those prevailing pre-war will show./
===
shown— *The suggestion is utterly untrue, as a comparison of present prices with those* prevailing pre-war *will show.*/
>>>

<<<
The difference is made up, though not, of course, to the same extent as prewar, by interest on our foreign investments./
===
*The difference is made up, though not, of course,* to the same extent as pre-war, *by interest on our foreign investments.*/
>>>

<<<
The season-ticket holder, too, is to pay about 75 per cent. more than he did pre-war./
===
*The season-ticket holder, too, is to pay about 75 per cent. more than* he did pre-war./
>>>

<<<
The number of houses demolished annually pre-war ` is again not accurately known.
===
*The number of houses* demolished annually pre-war *is again not accurately known.*
>>>

