<<<
primer. The traditional pronunciation is pri’‘mer, & the word was very commonly spelt with -mm-. This pronunciation is still used in the names of types; but in the names of modern school manuals pri‘mer is now more usual. primeur. See FRENCH WORDS. primeval, -aeval. The first is recommended; see Æ, Œ,
===
**primer.** The traditional pronunciation is prĭ'*mer*, & the word was very commonly spelt with *-mm-*. This pronunciation is still used in the names of types; but in the names of modern school manuals prī'*mer* is now more usual. **primeur.** See ^^FRENCH WORDS^^. **primeval, -aeval.** The first is recommended; see ^^Æ, Œ^^.
>>>
